          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em regular tesselation
            or
            %em tiling
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plane"} plane
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+polygons"} regular polygons
            (the tiles), so that polygons overlap only on their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
            and such the same number of tiles meet at each
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex"} vertex
          %p
            A tesselation by regular
            = succeed "-gons" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            of them meet at each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex"} vertex
            is denoted by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schl%C3%A4fli+symbol"} Schläfli symbol
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{n,k\}
          %h3#euclidean_tesselation Euclidean tesselation
          %p
            For example
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 3
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 6
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{3,6\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 4
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{4,4\}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 6
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{6,3\}
            denote the familiar tilings of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+plane"} Euclidean plane
            by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangles"} triangles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/squares"} squares
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hexagons"} hexagons
          %h3#hyperbolic_tesselations Hyperbolic tesselations
          %p
            Similarly a
            %em hyperbologic tesselation
            is such a tiling of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+plane"} hyperbolic plane
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+polygons"} regular polygons
          %p
            For example the hyperbolic tesselation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 5
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{5,4\}
            by
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pentagons"} pentagons
          %center
            %a{:href => "https://eschermath.org/mediawiki/upload/b/b5/Hyp-tess-5-4.png"}
              %img{:src => "https://eschermath.org/mediawiki/upload/b/b5/Hyp-tess-5-4.png", :width => "300"}/
          %p
            In discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+entanglement+entropy"} holographic entanglement entropy
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+error+correcting+codes"} quantum error correcting codes
            this controls the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HaPPY+code"} HaPPY code
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Majorana+dimer+code#JGPE19"} JGPE 19
          %p
            Or the hyperbolic tesselation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 4
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 6
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{4,6\}
            by
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/squares"} squares
          %center
            %a{:href => "hhttps://eschermath.org/mediawiki/upload/a/a4/Hyp-tess-4-6.png"}
              %img{:src => "https://eschermath.org/mediawiki/upload/a/a4/Hyp-tess-4-6.png", :width => "300"}/
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wallpaper+group"} wallpaper group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+entanglement+entropy"} holographic entanglement entropy
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p Introduction and survey:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Joyce"}> David Joyce
                ,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://mathcs.clarku.edu/~djoyce/poincare/index.html"} Hyperbolic Tesselations
            %li
              %p
                Damon Motz-Storey,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Constructing Hyperbolic Polygon Tessellations
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://damonmotzstorey.files.wordpress.com/2016/11/thesiswithrevisions_damonmotzstorey.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MotzStoreyTesselations.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tessellation"} Tesselation
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uniform_tilings_in_hyperbolic_plane"} Uniform tilings in hyperbolic plane
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://mathstat.slu.edu/escher/index.php\n/Hyperbolic_Geometry#Hyperbolic_Tessellations"} Hyperbolic Geometry – Hyperbolic Tesselations
          %p
            Claim of a hyperbolic tessalation approximated by a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/photonic+crystal"} photonic crystal
          %ul
            %li
              Alicia J. Kollár, Mattias Fitzpatrick, Andrew A. Houck,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Hyperbolic Lattices in Circuit Quantum Electrodynamics
              %strong 571
              (2019) 45–50 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.09549"}> arXiv:1802.09549
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-019-1348-3"} doi:10.1038/s41586-019-1348-3
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Latham Boyle, Justin Kulp:
              %em Holographic Foliations: Self-Similar Quasicrystals from Hyperbolic Honeycombs
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.15316"}> arXiv:2408.15316
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#via_inflation_rules Via inflation rules
          %p On iterative constructions of hyperbolic tesselations from “inflation rules”:
          %ul
            %li
              Latham Boyle, Madeline Dickens, Felix Flicker, Section IV of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Conformal Quasicrystals and Holography
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.02665"} arXiv:1805.02665
          %p following:
          %ul
            %li
              Latham Boyle, Paul J. Steinhardt,
              %em Self-Similar One-Dimensional Quasilattices
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1608.08220"}> arXiv:1608.08220
              )
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Jahn"}> Alexander Jahn
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zolt%C3%A1n+Zimbor%C3%A1s"} Zoltán Zimborás
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jens+Eisert"} Jens Eisert
              = succeed "," do
                %em Central charges of aperiodic holographic tensor network models
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.03485"} arXiv:1911.03485
        .revisedby
          %p
